==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pro-||*dʰeh₁-}}
From {{uder|en|la|proficiens}}, present participle of {{m|la|proficere||to go forward, advance, make progress, succeed, be profitable or useful}}, from {{m|la|pro||forth, forward}} + {{m|la|facere||to make, do}}; see {{m|en|fact}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈfɪʃ.ənt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɹoʊˈfɪʃ.ənt/|/pɹəˈfɪʃ.ənt/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-proficient.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪʃənt|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Good at something; [[skilled]]; [[fluent]]; [[practiced]], especially in relation to a task or skill.
#: {{ux|en|He was a '''proficient''' writer with an interest in human nature.}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Tarzan of the Apes|chapter=5|text=By constant playing and experimenting with these he learned to tie rude knots, and make sliding nooses; and with these he and the younger apes amused themselves. What Tarzan did they tried to do also, but he alone originated and became '''proficient'''.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|good at}} {{l|en|skilled}}, {{l|en|fluent}}, {{l|en|practiced}}

